Strict release evidence for issue #12

Generated locally in WSL Ubuntu from a clean source checkout on the task branch.
The validation, image-scan, and local-proof command groups ran concurrently.
The release-proof group ran after all three completed successfully.
Every recorded command group exited 0; no thresholds or sample artifacts were changed.

Scope: current local gateway conformance, static controls, image scans, and restore tooling.
Eval and safety reports use evidence_class=conformance with the mock runtime.
The load test uses the same mock runtime (2 VUs, 15 seconds).
The restore drill replays the repository synthetic two-key Redis AOF fixture into Docker.
The evidence pack is static (LIVE=0); no live Kubernetes or customer infrastructure was used.
Model quality, production performance, production-data recovery, and release signatures
are not established by this local run. The source CI run is contextual, not this run.
The gate enforces a 24-hour file-mtime freshness window; this is a dated snapshot.

Reproduction prerequisites: Linux/WSL, Python 3 with venv, GNU make, Git, a working
Docker Engine, Helm, and the strict tools in platform/tools/validation-toolchain.yaml.
The required CLIs were already installed. scripts/install-validation-tools.sh can
install missing strict tools; restore-drill installation requires Go.
Network access to public package/image registries, GitHub, Kubernetes schemas, and
the Trivy database is needed. No cloud account or external model API key is needed.

